From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sun, 08 Nov 2026 08:38:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: npu: order the tx descriptor writes before the done bit

A done bit in a control word hands its tx slot to the NPU, which then
reads TXWI copy and buffer address from that slot. Without a barrier,
a done bit can become visible before its TXWI stores land, and the
NPU reads a TXWI that holds parts of the previous frame of that slot.
Its token belongs by then to a live frame in another slot, because a
freed token goes to a new frame at once. Firmware reports this token
for the sent frame, so the host frees the token of the live frame, and
firmware never reports the own token of the sent frame. That token
stays allocated until a stale token check resets the band.

A dma_wmb() before the control word orders these writes, as the
register write of a ring kick does for a regular queue.

Fixes: 141a81557070 ("wifi: mt76: Introduce the NPU generic layer")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 npu.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -229,6 +229,8 @@ int mt76_npu_dma_add_buf(struct mt76_phy
 	/* TODO: Take into account unlinear skbs */
 	memcpy(desc[q->head].txwi, txwi_ptr, txwi_len);
 	desc[q->head].addr = buf->addr;
+	/* the NPU takes the slot at the done bit, not at the queue kick */
+	dma_wmb();
 	desc[q->head].ctrl = FIELD_PREP(NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_VEND_LEN_MASK, txwi_len) |
 			     FIELD_PREP(NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_LEN_MASK, skb->len) |
 			     NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK;
